## Shadow baseline live image
##
## Software selection: ONLY kali-linux-core + kali-desktop-xfce.
## kali-desktop-live is included because it provides live-boot / live-config,
## which are required for the live system to actually boot (priority #1:
## boot reliability). It is part of Kali's live-boot system, not an extra
## security tool / application.
##
## $ ./build.sh --variant shadow

## Base Kali system + live-boot / live-config (required for live boot)
kali-linux-core
kali-desktop-live

## Lightweight XFCE desktop
kali-desktop-xfce

## Display manager (auto-login for the shadow user, see common lightdm.conf)
lightdm
lightdm-gtk-greeter

## Default shell + terminal (matches terminal-note: zsh is the live user's
## shell, xfce4-terminal the x-terminal-emulator for the xfce variant)
zsh
xfce4-terminal

## Fonts: Fira Code is the default for all normal/bold text, Cantarell for UI
## and URW base35 as fallback. fonts-dejavu-core guarantees the ☯ prompt glyph
## (U+262F, not present in Fira Code) and its box-drawing glyphs. Noto Egyptian
## Hieroglyphs (extracted from fonts-noto-core by
## hooks/live/install-noto-glyphs.chroot, package then discarded) is
## fallback-only for Egyptian glyphs. fonts-noto-core is NOT installed; the
## extra + CJK sets are too large to keep.
fonts-firacode
fonts-urw-base35
fonts-mathjax
fonts-cantarell
fonts-dejavu-core
xfonts-utils
xfonts-encodings

## Thunar file manager extras - volume management, drive/USB auto-mount
thunar-volman
thunar-archive-plugin
gvfs
gvfs-backends
udisks2

## Wireless networking - NetworkManager (with nm-applet tray icon), WPA
## supplicant and rfkill control. network-manager-applet provides the applet;
## the old transitional network-manager-gnome name does not exist in Kali.
network-manager
network-manager-applet
wpasupplicant
rfkill

## Audio - modern lightweight PipeWire stack
pipewire
wireplumber

## Polkit daemon (desktop privilege handling)
polkitd

## zram swap for low-RAM hardware
systemd-zram-generator

## No extra Kali metapackages, security tools, applications, or utilities
## at the baseline stage. Optimizations are added in later stages, each
## measured against this baseline.
